                        <provenance>The manuscript belonged originally to <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC2248DabraB">Dabra Bǝrhān Śǝllāse</placeName> in or near 
                            <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC3577Gondar">Gondar</placeName>. Later, it belonged to <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0101MadhaneAlam">Madḫāne ʿĀlam</placeName> of
                            <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS9430Tewodros">Tewodros II</persName>. It was taken at <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC4547Maqdal">Maqdalā</placeName> in 
                            <date when="1868">1868</date> (cf. <ref target="#e1"/>) by a soldier whose name is carved in the wooden cover.
                            After being brought to England the manuscript belonged to <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15047HeygateL">Anna F. A.
                        Heygate Lambert</persName>,
                            and to <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS1027Garratts">Garratts Hall Library</placeName>. 
                            Bought by the <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0775LWC">Wellcome Institute</placeName> in <date when="1919"/>.
                                </provenance>
